TYPES.md §9.1: the keys of a keyed list are unique, checked at evaluation: a computed key that
repeats an earlier one is reported at the second, naming the first.
-- teamboard/farm.canon --
package teamboard

record Level {
  level: Int
  cost: Int
}

record Farm {
  levels: [Level] keyed by level
}

let farm: Farm = { levels: [{ level: 1, cost: 10 }, { level: 2, cost: 20 }, { level: 0 + 1, cost: 30 }] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3102]  teamboard/farm.canon:12:86
  farm.levels[1].level: key 1 is used twice (first at teamboard/farm.canon:12)
  expected by teamboard/farm.canon:9 (levels: [Level] keyed by level)

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
